# Opinion

Meeting: 0009-design-web-client-architecture
Agent: Critic
Task: design web client architecture
Context:
- Without a backend wire-up, we risk letting the JS model drift from the Python source of truth.
Position:
- Keep validation messages and shape close to backend semantics; no silent coercions.
- Avoid clever abstractions that hide time parsing or mutate shared state implicitly.
Recommendations:
- Normalize inputs aggressively (trim names, owners, tags) and throw descriptive errors early.
- Keep palette and seed data deterministic so tests don't flake on random IDs.
- Document assumptions in comments for future API integration.
